          "question": "e-7312",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Suppose that the value $V(t)$ of a particular car can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d V}{\\textrm d t} = -0.1V,\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in years, since the car was first purchased. If the car was purchased for $\\[math]10\\,000,$ what will it be worth after $3$ years?",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037533/example-7312.json",
          "file_sha256": "8e1d9a5d68f9ef6ab12efb437bb6a5d121eafb8e54b9d9f4019c1a949c4eacb3"
        }
      ],
